    "description": "## Diagnosis Batch\n\nUploads **multiple dental images** in a single request and returns a **batch of AI diagnosis results** for each uploaded image.\n\n- **Method:** `POST`\n- **URL:** `{{BASE_BACKEND_URL}}/diagnosis/batch`\n- **Content-Type:** `multipart/form-data`\n\n---\n\n### Purpose\nUse this endpoint to:\n- Submit multiple dental images at once.\n- Receive per-image diagnosis output including detection metadata and image URLs.\n\n---\n\n### Authentication\nThis request uses **Bearer Token** authentication.\n\n- Header:\n  - `Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}`\n\n> Ensure `{{authToken}}` is a valid JWT/access token issued by your backend.\n\n---\n\n### Required Variables\nSet these variables at the **collection** (or active environment) level:\n\n- `BASE_BACKEND_URL` — Base backend URL, e.g. `http://localhost:3000/api`\n- `authToken` — Bearer token used for `Authorization`\n\n---\n\n### Request Body\n**Body type:** `multipart/form-data`\n\n| Key | Type | Required | Description |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| `images` | file | Yes | One or more image files. Add multiple files using the same key (`images`). |\n\n**Notes**\n- Postman: choose **Body → form-data**, set key `images` to **File**, then click **Select Files** (you can add multiple rows with the same key or select multiple files if supported).\n\n---\n\n### Example cURL\n```bash\ncurl --location \"{{BASE_BACKEND_URL}}/diagnosis/batch\" \\\n  --header \"Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}\" \\\n  --form \"images=@/path/to/image1.jpg\" \\\n  --form \"images=@/path/to/image2.jpg\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Response (Schema Overview)\nTypical successful response includes a `diagnoses` array. Each item corresponds to one uploaded image.\n\n**Top-level**\n- `diagnoses` (array)\n\n**diagnoses[]**\n- `inputImageUrl` (string | null) — relative/absolute URL to the uploaded input image\n- `outputImageUrl` (string | null) — relative/absolute URL to the generated/annotated output image\n- `detectionResults` (object | null)\n\n**diagnoses[].detectionResults** (commonly used fields)\n- `filename` (string)\n- `urgency_level` (string | number)\n- `report` (string)\n\n> Additional fields may be present depending on backend/AI version.\n\n---\n\n### Common Errors\n- **400 Bad Request**\n  - Missing `images` key, invalid form-data, or unsupported file type.\n- **401 Unauthorized**\n  - Missing/invalid/expired `authToken`.\n\n---\n\n### Visualizer Notes (Images Base URL)\nThis request includes a **Postman Visualizer** in the **Tests** tab to display the batch results with images.\n\n- The script currently prepends a hardcoded base URL:\n  - `http://localhost:3000`\n- It builds image sources like:\n  - `http://localhost:3000` + `inputImageUrl`\n  - `http://localhost:3000` + `outputImageUrl`\n\nIf your backend is not running at `http://localhost:3000`, update the visualizer base in the script (or align your server/base URLs accordingly).",
