            "description": "## Purpose\n\nUploads a dental image (or related diagnostic file) and returns an AI-generated diagnostic report, urgency assessment, and detection results (including an annotated image when available).\n\n## Endpoint\n\n- **Method:** `POST`\n    \n- **URL:** `http://localhost:8000/diagnose`\n    \n\n## Authentication\n\n- **Auth:** None.\n    \n\n## Required Headers\n\n- `Accept: application/json`\n    \n\n> Note: When sending `multipart/form-data`, Postman/cURL will set the correct `Content-Type` boundary automatically. Avoid manually forcing `Content-Type: application/json` for this request. \n  \n\n## Request Body\n\n- **Type:** `multipart/form-data`\n    \n- **Fields:**\n    - `file` (**required**): The image/file to be analyzed.\n        \n\n## Response (JSON) Schema\n\nSuccessful response returns JSON with the following key fields:\n\n- `status` (string): e.g. `\"success\"`.\n    \n- `report` (string): Narrative analysis / findings summary.\n    \n- `urgency_level` (string): e.g. `\"low\" | \"medium\" | \"high\"`.\n    \n- `action_plan` (string\\[\\]): List of recommended next steps.\n    \n- `detection` (object):\n    - `detections` (array): List of detected conditions.\n        - `label` (string): Condition name.\n            \n        - `confidence` (number): Confidence score (0–1).\n            \n    - `classification` (object/map): Map of class name → score/probability.\n        - Example keys: `\"Calculus\"`, `\"Dental Caries\"`, `\"Tooth Discoloration\"`, etc.\n            \n    - `detection_image` (string, base64): Base64-encoded annotated image (typically PNG). May be empty/missing if not produced.\n        \n\n## Example cURL\n\n``` bash\ncurl --request POST \"http://localhost:8000/diagnose\" \\\n  --header \"Accept: application/json\" \\\n  --form \"file=@/path/to/image.png\"\n\n ```"
