            "description": "## Purpose\nSend a user question plus model/diagnostic context to the backend chat endpoint and receive an AI-generated answer.\n\n## Endpoint\n- **Method:** `POST`\n- **URL:** `localhost:8000/chat`\n\n> Note: This endpoint targets **localhost**, so it will only work when the API server is running on your machine (or you are tunneling/port-forwarding to a machine running it).\n\n## Headers\n| Header | Value | Required | Description |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| `Content-Type` | `application/json` | Yes | Request body is JSON. |\n| `Accept` | `application/json` | Recommended | Client expects JSON back. |\n\n## Request body\n**Content-Type:** `application/json`\n\n### Schema\n```json\n{\n  \"question\": \"string\",\n  \"context\": \"string\"\n}\n```\n\n### Fields\n- `question` *(string, required)*: The end-user question to ask.\n- `context` *(string, required)*: Supporting context for the model (e.g., diagnosis/classification output, detected findings, notes).\n\n## Example request\n```json\n{\n  \"question\": \"What should I do about my cavities?\",\n  \"context\": \"Classification: caries (85%). Detected: ...\"\n}\n```\n\n## Successful response\n### `200 OK`\nReturns an answer payload.\n\n**Response body (shape):**\n```json\n{\n  \"answer\": \"string\"\n}\n```\n\n**Example (from a recent run):**\n```json\n{\n  \"answer\": \"Based on your dental report, you have de...\"\n}\n```\n\n## Error responses (generic)\nThe exact error format depends on the backend implementation, but you may see:\n- **`400 Bad Request`**: Missing/invalid JSON or required fields (`question`, `context`).\n- **`415 Unsupported Media Type`**: `Content-Type` not set to `application/json`.\n- **`500 Internal Server Error`**: Unhandled server-side error.\n\n## Notes / Tips\n- **Localhost usage:** If the server is running on a different machine/container, update the host/port accordingly.\n- **Variableization suggestion:** Consider using a base URL variable (e.g., `{{url}}`) so this request can be run against different environments (local/dev/staging/prod) without editing the request. *(This is a suggestion only; no request changes are made here.)\n"
