            "description": "## Diagnose Batch\n\nUploads multiple dental images and returns an AI-powered diagnostic result for each file (report, urgency, action plan, and detection outputs). This endpoint is intended for **batch processing** of images in a single request.\n\n---\n\n## Endpoint\n\n- **Method:** `POST`\n- **URL:** `{{url}}/diagnose-batch`\n\n> Current saved URL in this request tab: `localhost:8000/diagnose-batch`  \n> Consider using the `{{url}}` variable for portability across environments.\n\n---\n\n## Headers\n\n| Header | Value | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Accept` | `application/json` | Response is JSON |\n| `Content-Type` | `multipart/form-data` | Required when sending files (Postman will set the boundary automatically) |\n\n> Note: If `Content-Type: application/json` is present, remove/disable it for this request. File uploads must use `multipart/form-data`.\n\n---\n\n## Request Body\n\n**Body type:** `multipart/form-data`\n\nAdd one or more image files using a repeatable form-data key:\n\n- **Key:** `files`\n- **Type:** `File`\n- **Repeatable:** Yes (add multiple `files` rows)\n\nExample (conceptual):\n\n```\nfiles: <TOOTH4.jpg>\nfiles: <TOOTH3.jpg>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Response\n\n**Content-Type:** `application/json`\n\n### Response schema (shape)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success | error\",\n  \"count\": 0,\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"filename\": \"string\",\n      \"report\": \"string\",\n      \"urgency_level\": \"low | medium | high\",\n      \"action_plan\": [\"string\"],\n      \"detection\": {\n        \"detections\": [\n          { \"label\": \"string\", \"confidence\": 0.0 }\n        ],\n        \"classification\": { \"<className>\": 0.0 },\n        \"detection_image\": \"<base64 png>\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Field meanings\n\n- `status`: Overall execution status.\n- `count`: Number of processed files returned in `results`.\n- `results[]`: Per-file output.\n  - `filename`: Original filename.\n  - `report`: Generated narrative summary.\n  - `urgency_level`: Triage level derived from findings.\n  - `action_plan[]`: Recommended next actions.\n  - `detection`:\n    - `detections[]`: Primary detected label(s) with confidence.\n    - `classification`: Class → probability map.\n    - `detection_image`: Base64-encoded PNG showing detection overlay/visual output (may be missing).\n\n---\n\n## Example response (snippet)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"count\": 2,\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"filename\": \"TOOTH4.jpg\",\n      \"urgency_level\": \"high\",\n      \"action_plan\": [\"...\"],\n      \"detection\": {\n        \"detections\": [{ \"label\": \"Caries Gingivitis\", \"confidence\": 0.6766 }],\n        \"classification\": { \"Caries Gingivitis\": 0.9971 },\n        \"detection_image\": \"iVBORw0KGgoAAA...\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Visualizer\n\nThis request includes a **Tests** script that uses `pm.visualizer.set()` to render a card for each item in `results` and display the detection image:\n\n- If `detection.detection_image` is present, it is rendered as:\n  - `data:image/png;base64,{{detection.detection_image}}`\n- If missing, the visualizer shows a “No image available” message.\n\nTo see it after sending the request, open the response’s **Visualize** tab."
          },
