                "description": "Registers a new user account.\n\n## Endpoint\n`POST {{BASE_BACKEND_URL}}/auth/register`\n\n## What it does\nCreates a new user using the provided **name**, **email**, and **password**.\n\nTypical usage:\n- Use this request first to create a user.\n- Then use your **Login** request (if available) to obtain an access token for authenticated endpoints.\n\n---\n\n## Required headers\nThis request expects JSON.\n\n| Header | Value | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| `Accept` | `application/json` | Yes | Response is JSON. |\n| `Content-Type` | `application/json` | Yes | Body must be JSON. |\n\n---\n\n## Request body (JSON)\n\n### Schema\n```json\n{\n  \"email\": \"string\",\n  \"name\": \"string\",\n  \"password\": \"string\"\n}\n```\n\n### Field meanings\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| `email` | string | Yes | User’s email address (should be unique). |\n| `name` | string | Yes | User’s display/full name. |\n| `password` | string | Yes | User password. |\n\n### Validation rules (expected)\nExact rules can vary by implementation, but common validations for this endpoint:\n- `email`: must be a valid email format.\n- `email`: must be unique (if already registered, expect a 400 response).\n- `name`: must be non-empty.\n- `password`: must be non-empty and meet minimum length (commonly 6+ characters).\n\n---\n\n## Example request\n```http\nPOST {{BASE_BACKEND_URL}}/auth/register\nAccept: application/json\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"email\": \"user1@gmail.com\",\n  \"name\": \"User One\",\n  \"password\": \"123456\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Example responses\n\n### 201 Created (example)\n> Response shape may differ depending on your backend.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"message\": \"User registered successfully\"\n}\n```\n\n### 400 Bad Request (example)\nCommon causes:\n- Invalid payload (missing/invalid fields)\n- Email already exists\n\n```json\n{\n  \"message\": \"Bad Request\"\n}\n```\n\nFor a more specific case, see the saved example: **\"400 - Email already exists\"**.\n\n---\n\n## Notes on `{{BASE_BACKEND_URL}}`\n- `{{BASE_BACKEND_URL}}` is a variable that should point to the base URL of your backend API.\n- Example values:\n  - Local: `http://localhost/api`\n  - Dev/Staging/Prod: your deployed base URL\n- Ensure the correct environment/collection variable is active before sending.\n\n---\n\n## Using this in a Collection Runner (data-driven)\nTo run registrations for multiple users:\n1. Create a CSV/JSON data file with columns/keys: `email`, `name`, `password`.\n2. Update the request body to use iteration variables:\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n     \"name\": \"{{name}}\",\n     \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n   }\n   ```\n3. Run the collection/folder in the Collection Runner with your data file.\n\nTip: Use unique emails per iteration to avoid 400 errors for duplicates."
