                "description": "Logs a user into SMART-AI-DENTAL and returns an access token (and/or related auth payload) to authenticate subsequent requests.\n\n## Endpoint\n`POST {{BASE_BACKEND_URL}}/auth/login`\n\n## Required headers\n- `Accept: application/json`\n- `Content-Type: application/json`\n\n## Request body schema\nJSON object:\n- `email` *(string, required)* — User email address.\n- `password` *(string, required)* — User password.\n- `device_name` *(string, optional)* — Device/client identifier (useful for token naming or multi-device sessions, if supported by the backend).\n\n### Example — valid\n```json\n{\n  \"email\": \"owner@gmail.com\",\n  \"password\": \"owner123456\",\n  \"device_name\": \"architecto\"\n}\n```\n\n### Example — invalid (missing password)\n```json\n{\n  \"email\": \"owner@gmail.com\"\n}\n```\n\n### Example — invalid (wrong credentials)\n```json\n{\n  \"email\": \"owner@gmail.com\",\n  \"password\": \"wrong-password\"\n}\n```\n\n## Response overview\n> Exact response shape can vary by implementation. Use the status code + JSON body to determine next steps.\n\n### `200 OK`\n- Login succeeded.\n- Response typically includes an access token (and possibly token type, user data, expiration, etc.).\n- Use the returned token in subsequent protected endpoints (commonly via `Authorization: Bearer <token>`).\n\n### `400 Bad Request`\n- Validation error (e.g., missing/invalid fields such as `email` format or missing `password`).\n- Response commonly includes an error message and/or validation details.\n\n### `401 Unauthorized`\n- Authentication failed (e.g., incorrect email/password).\n- Response commonly includes an error message indicating invalid credentials.\n\n## Notes\n- This request uses the environment/collection variable `{{BASE_BACKEND_URL}}`. Make sure it is set to the correct backend base URL (for example `http://localhost/api` or your deployed URL) before sending.\n- After a successful login (`200`), store the returned token in a variable for reuse in other requests (for example, set an environment variable like `token` and reference it later as `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`)."
