                "description": "## Diagnosis\n\nUploads a dental image for AI-assisted diagnosis and returns URLs for the original (input) and processed (output) images.\n\n### Endpoint\n- **Method:** `POST`\n- **URL:** `{{BASE_BACKEND_URL}}/diagnosis`\n\n### Authentication\nThis endpoint requires **Bearer Token** authentication.\n\n- Token source: `{{authToken}}`\n- Header format:\n  ```http\n  Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}\n  ```\n\n### Request Body\nSend a `multipart/form-data` payload with the following required field:\n\n- `image` (**file**, required): the image to be diagnosed.\n\n### Response\nOn success, the response contains a `diagnosis` object with image URLs.\n\nTypical shape:\n```json\n{\n  \"diagnosis\": {\n    \"inputImageUrl\": \"<string>\",\n    \"outputImageUrl\": \"<string>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- `diagnosis.inputImageUrl`: URL/path to the uploaded original image\n- `diagnosis.outputImageUrl`: URL/path to the processed/annotated image (if generated)\n\n### Common Errors\n- **400 Bad Request**: missing/invalid `image` form field, unsupported file, or validation errors.\n- **401 Unauthorized**: missing/invalid/expired `{{authToken}}`.\n\n### Visualizer Note\nThis request includes a **Visualizer** that displays an **Input vs Output** image comparison based on `diagnosis.inputImageUrl` and `diagnosis.outputImageUrl`. After sending the request, open the **Visualizer** view in the response pane to see the side-by-side images."
