                "description": "## Chat Endpoint\n\n### Purpose\nSubmits a question to the AI diagnostic system for a specific diagnosis session and retrieves an AI-generated answer based on the diagnosis context.\n\n### HTTP Method & Endpoint\n```\nPOST {{BASE_BACKEND_URL}}/chat/:diagnosis_id\n```\n\n### Path Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description | Example |\n|-----------|------|-------------|---------|\n| `diagnosis_id` | string | The unique identifier of the diagnosis session to which the question belongs | `69b5b305cb5d2a484a741f67` |\n\n### Request Headers\n\n| Header | Value | Purpose |\n|--------|-------|---------|\n| `Accept` | `application/json` | Specifies that the client expects a JSON response |\n| `Content-Type` | `application/json` | Indicates that the request body contains JSON data |\n\n### Request Body\n\nThe request body should be a JSON object with the following structure:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"question\": \"string\"\n}\n```\n\n**Fields:**\n- `question` (string, required): The question to ask the AI diagnostic system regarding the diagnosis\n\n**Example:**\n```json\n{\n  \"question\": \"so what is the next step\"\n}\n```\n\n### Response Structure\n\n**Status Code:** 200 OK\n\n**Response Body:**\n```json\n{\n  \"diagnosis_id\": \"string\",\n  \"last_active\": \"ISO 8601 timestamp\",\n  \"question\": \"string\",\n  \"answer\": \"string\"\n}\n```\n\n**Fields:**\n- `diagnosis_id` (string): The identifier of the diagnosis session\n- `last_active` (string): ISO 8601 timestamp of when the diagnosis was last active\n- `question` (string): The question that was submitted\n- `answer` (string): The AI-generated answer to the question\n\n**Example Response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"diagnosis_id\": \"69b5b305cb5d2a484a741f67\",\n  \"last_active\": \"2026-03-14T19:14:09.907Z\",\n  \"question\": \"so what is the next step\",\n  \"answer\": \"To help manage the inflammation around y...\"\n}\n```\n\n### Error Responses\n\n#### 400 - Bad Request\nReturned when the request body is malformed or missing required fields.\n\n**Example:** See the \"400 - Bad Request\" saved example for details.\n\n#### 400 - Bad Request - Diagnosis ID Invalid\nReturned when the provided `diagnosis_id` path parameter is invalid or does not exist in the system.\n\n**Example:** See the \"400 - Bad Request - Diagnosis ID Invalid\" saved example for details.\n\n### Important Notes & Usage Guidelines\n\n- **Authentication:** Ensure that the `authToken` variable is properly set in your environment before making requests\n- **Base URL:** The `BASE_BACKEND_URL` variable must be configured in your environment (e.g., set to `http://localhost/api` or your production URL)\n- **Diagnosis Session:** The `diagnosis_id` must correspond to an existing diagnosis session; invalid IDs will result in a 400 error\n- **Question Format:** Keep questions clear and concise for better AI responses\n- **Response Time:** The AI may take a few seconds to generate a response; consider setting appropriate timeout values\n- **Rate Limiting:** Be aware of any rate limits imposed by the backend service when submitting multiple questions in succession"
